:0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"This isn't a huge deal, but it seems a little odd:\n\n``` python\nIn [1]: import pandas as pd\n\nIn [2]: a = pd.SparseArray([True, False, False, False, True], fill_value=False, dtype=bool)\n\nIn [3]: a\nOut[3]: \n[True, False, False, False, True]\nFill: False\nIntIndex\nIndices: array([0, 4], dtype=int32)\n\nIn [4]: a.dtype\nOut[4]: dtype('bool')\n\nIn [5]: d = a.to_dense()\n\nIn [6]: d\nOut[6]: array([ 1.,  0.,  0.,  0.,  1.])\n\nIn [7]: d.dtype\nOut[7]: dtype('float64')\n```\n\nI would have expected `d` to retain the dtype of `bool`. I can cast down, but I am still wasting 7 bytes per element in the process. \n","closed_by":{"login":"jreback","id":953992,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1Mzk5Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/953992?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback","html_url":"https://github.com/jreback","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jreback/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/10648/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/10648/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}